      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Martyrdom Device" hidden="false" id="239a-64ac-6630-4b01">
          <constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="0e04-c99e-1e80-4b01" includeChildSelections="false"/><constraint type="max" value="4" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="430b-7755-f37c-4b01" includeChildSelections="true"/></constraints>
          <costs><cost name="Ducats" typeId="8d43-33fd-332d-17a6" value="25"/><cost name="Glory Points" typeId="f3bb-a7e6-d476-f60b" value="0"/></costs>
          <profiles><profile name="Awaited" typeId="058c-866b-6487-ccc4" typeName="Ability" hidden="false" id="0d80-57cc-d681-4b01"><characteristics><characteristic name="Description" typeId="2ecd-b4ff-9e78-a8e2">Awaited: If an Ecclesiastic Prisoner is taken Out of Action when their Martyrdom Device is triggered, do not count this towards the number of models from the Warband that have been taken Out of Action for Morale Checks.</characteristic></characteristics></profile><profile name="Martyrdom Device" typeId="7079-589c-df69-fa7e" typeName="Battlekit" hidden="false" id="6e13-b490-6574-4b02"><characteristics><characteristic name="Type" typeId="3f15-74a1-4d35-3642">Equipment</characteristic><characteristic name="Range" typeId="2b32-2f45-9c06-7a77">-</characteristic><characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="5093-5528-b08f-1496">BLAST 3&quot;, SHRAPNEL</characteristic><characteristic name="Rules" typeId="4834-43a9-1c93-9062">Detonate ACTION: An Ecclesiastic Prisoner with a Martyrdom Device can take a Detonate ACTION. If they do so, the Martyrdom Device detonates and cannot be used again. When a Martyrdom Device detonates, all models (friend or foe) within 3&quot; of the Ecclesiastic Prisoner taking the Detonate ACTION and in its Line of Sight are hit by a Ranged Attack with the SHRAPNEL Keyword. Add +1 INJURY DICE to the Injury Rolls for models that are within 1&quot; of the Ecclesiastic Prisoner taking the Detonate ACTION. Seek Martyrdom: When an Ecclesiastic Prisoner takes a Detonate ACTION, make an Injury Roll for the Ecclesiastic Prisoner by rolling 4D6 and adding all 4 dice together. If an Ecclesiastic Prisoner detonates their Martyrdom Device and survives the game, you must either buy them a new Martyrdom Device for 25 ducats, or use them without one.</characteristic></characteristics></profile></profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Minenhelm" hidden="true" id="c4bc-74f7-e224-4b02">
          <constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="4512-c6c3-bb7a-4b02" includeChildSelections="false"/></constraints>
          <costs><cost name="Ducats" typeId="8d43-33fd-332d-17a6" value="10"/><cost name="Glory Points" typeId="f3bb-a7e6-d476-f60b" value="0"/></costs>
          <profiles><profile name="Minenhelm" typeId="7079-589c-df69-fa7e" typeName="Battlekit" hidden="false" id="0d80-57cc-d681-4b02"><characteristics><characteristic name="Type" typeId="3f15-74a1-4d35-3642">Equipment</characteristic><characteristic name="Range" typeId="2b32-2f45-9c06-7a77">-</characteristic><characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="5093-5528-b08f-1496">-</characteristic><characteristic name="Rules" typeId="4834-43a9-1c93-9062">Last Act: Add +1 INJURY DICE to the Injury Rolls for models that are within 1&quot; of an Ecclesiastic Prisoner with a Minenhelm when it takes a Detonate ACTION (for a total of +2 INJURY DICE instead of +1). Ecclesiastic Prisoners that have a Minenhelm are automatically killed when their Martyrdom Device detonates. Minenhelm Slam: An Ecclesiastic Prisoner that has a Minenhelm can make a Melee Attack even though they do not have a Melee Weapon.</characteristic></characteristics></profile></profiles>
          <modifiers><modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden"><conditions><condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" childId="239a-64ac-6630-4b01" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/></conditions></modifier></modifiers>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <costs><cost name="Ducats" typeId="8d43-33fd-332d-17a6" value="20"/><cost name="Glory Points" typeId="f3bb-a7e6-d476-f60b" value="0"/></costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Anchorite Shrine" hidden="false" id="4ed5-3209-4bf7-4b02">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Anchorite Shrine" typeId="b3af-94f9-2e35-d1c5" typeName="Unit" hidden="false" id="1104-c3e9-7172-4b02"><characteristics><characteristic name="Movement" typeId="b725-e0a4-16ae-8df2">6&quot;/Infantry</characteristic><characteristic name="Ranged" typeId="1a4f-d2cd-c405-6200">-</characteristic><characteristic name="Melee" typeId="12e8-ff8c-c933-9eb5">+2 DICE</characteristic><characteristic name="Armour" typeId="5de9-d70e-9021-6f71">-3</characteristic><characteristic name="Base" typeId="73ae-cc17-596e-0481">60mm</characteristic></characteristics></profile>
        <profile name="Bonebreaker Mace" typeId="090c-b12e-592a-9874" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="a28a-9034-856e-4b02"><characteristics><characteristic name="Type" typeId="f90e-171a-4ca6-3845">1-Handed</characteristic><characteristic name="Range" typeId="31a7-b5e8-41dc-5fd1">Melee</characteristic><characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="8cd6-8018-f2da-5ede">+1 INJURY DICE, RISKY</characteristic><characteristic name="Rules" typeId="87f0-637b-734a-22eb">-</characteristic></characteristics></profile>
        <profile name="Catherine Wheel" typeId="090c-b12e-592a-9874" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="239a-64ac-6630-4b02"><characteristics><characteristic name="Type" typeId="f90e-171a-4ca6-3845">1-Handed</characteristic><characteristic name="Range" typeId="31a7-b5e8-41dc-5fd1">Melee</characteristic><characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="8cd6-8018-f2da-5ede">+1 DICE, DEADLY, HEAVY, RISKY</characteristic><characteristic name="Rules" typeId="87f0-637b-734a-22eb">-</characteristic></characteristics></profile>
        <profile name="Broken on the Wheel" typeId="058c-866b-6487-ccc4" typeName="Ability" hidden="false" id="0e04-c99e-1e80-4b02"><characteristics><characteristic name="Description" typeId="2ecd-b4ff-9e78-a8e2">Broken on the Wheel: At the start of each game, before deployment, you can say that one Leper-Pilgrim or Ecclesiastic Prisoner will be broken on the wheel to show their piety and devotion. The model you choose is permanently removed from your Warband, but in a campaign you can redistribute their Battlekit to other models that would be allowed to have it in the following Quartermaster Step. The Anchorite Shrine then shatters the bones of the volunteer and carries the broken victim to battle upon its great wheel. Injuries that would be inflicted on the Anchorite Shrine are instead inflicted on its unfortunate victim, until the victim finally passes away. Until the Shrine suffers an Out of Action result on the Injury Table, it has an Armour Characteristic of 0, does not have the NEGATE SHRAPNEL and TOUGH Keywords, treats Down results as Minor Hit results, and treats its first Out of Action result as No Effect. When that happens, remove any BLOOD MARKERS from the Shrine; from then on, these special rules no longer apply, it has an Armour Characteristic of -3, and gains the NEGATE SHRAPNEL and TOUGH Keywords (TOUGH applies the next time the Shrine suffers an Out of Action result on the Injury Table).</characteristic></characteristics></profile>
        <profile name="Symphony of Slaughter" typeId="058c-866b-6487-ccc4" typeName="Ability" hidden="false" id="430b-7755-f37c-4b02"><characteristics><characteristic name="Description" typeId="2ecd-b4ff-9e78-a8e2">Symphony of Slaughter: An Anchorite Shrine is armed with two 1-Handed Melee Weapons (the Catherine Wheel and a Bonebreaker Mace). When it makes a Melee Attack, it can either attack once using either weapon, or twice, first with the Catherine Wheel and second with its Bonebreaker Mace (the Off-Hand Weapon modifier applies to the attack made with the Bonebreaker Mace). Both weapons have the RISKY Keyword.</characteristic></characteristics></profile>
      </profiles>
      <constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="6e13-b490-6574-4b03" includeChildSelections="true"/></constraints>
